      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city sits on the historic James River & Kanawha Turnpike, later called the Midland Trail, a major 19th‑century travel route.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wvencyclopedia.org/entries/489",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Thomas Memorial Hospital, founded in 1946, has served South Charleston and the surrounding region for more than seven decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
